1
00:00:00,328 --> 00:00:01,328
(All characters and organizations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,398 --> 00:00:02,768
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,828 --> 00:00:03,828
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:07,198 --> 00:00:08,338
Where are you right now?

5
00:00:11,478 --> 00:00:12,508
Where are you?

6
00:00:17,548 --> 00:00:18,578
I'm sorry.

7
00:00:18,848 --> 00:00:20,578
Well, as for Gyeol,

8
00:00:21,448 --> 00:00:24,718
my brother is going to pick him up tomorrow morning.

9
00:00:25,688 --> 00:00:27,358
If you could just send me the address...

10
00:00:27,828 --> 00:00:29,058
Gyu Rim, where are you?

11
00:00:35,528 --> 00:00:36,668
I'm coming to you now.

12
00:00:42,308 --> 00:00:43,638
I'm on my way to you.

13
00:00:43,968 --> 00:00:45,008
Where are you?

14
00:00:53,848 --> 00:00:54,848
Gyu Rim.

15
00:00:59,658 --> 00:01:01,088
Don't come, Mu Jin.

16
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:05,958
Later.

17
00:01:08,898 --> 00:01:10,028
Later.

18
00:01:12,898 --> 00:01:14,708
Please take care of Gyeol.

19
00:01:18,338 --> 00:01:19,378
I'm sorry.

20
00:01:20,738 --> 00:01:22,448
I'm so sorry, Mu Jin.

21
00:01:47,708 --> 00:01:48,738
What's going on?

22
00:01:50,968 --> 00:01:54,478
Why is Han Gyeol washing his face in our bathroom?

23
00:01:58,218 --> 00:01:59,218
Hey.

24
00:01:59,278 --> 00:02:01,818
I know you own 70 percent of this place,

25
00:02:02,418 --> 00:02:03,418
but don't you think...

26
00:02:03,488 --> 00:02:04,488
you owe your roommate an explanation?

27
00:02:06,118 --> 00:02:07,188
Something came up.

28
00:02:07,758 --> 00:02:11,098
- I'll explain later. - Don't tell me later. Explain now.

29
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,298
Jung Woo.

30
00:02:13,598 --> 00:02:15,028
I'll explain.

31
00:02:21,108 --> 00:02:22,268
I have...

32
00:02:22,508 --> 00:02:24,878
a secret about my birth.

33
00:02:28,578 --> 00:02:31,378
That's why I'm here at your place.

34
00:02:35,118 --> 00:02:36,688
Don't tell me you told the kid everything.

35
00:02:36,748 --> 00:02:37,758
Like, "I am your father."

36
00:02:37,818 --> 00:02:39,358
Gosh. It's not like that.

37
00:02:40,318 --> 00:02:41,528
If it's not that, then what is it?

38
00:02:43,158 --> 00:02:44,828
My mom...

39
00:02:45,528 --> 00:02:47,358
is not my birth mother.

40
00:02:50,498 --> 00:02:51,498
Gyeol,

41
00:02:52,398 --> 00:02:53,568
you don't have to explain...

42
00:02:53,638 --> 00:02:56,168
every little thing to a guy like him, okay?

43
00:02:57,008 --> 00:02:58,338
Let's go to our room.

44
00:03:01,478 --> 00:03:02,908
Did you bring any lotion?

45
00:03:03,708 --> 00:03:05,248
Do you want to use mine?

46
00:03:08,188 --> 00:03:12,458
Gyu Rim isn't Gyeol's birth mother? Then, what about Mu Jin?

47
00:03:13,288 --> 00:03:15,858
Then that means Mu Jin isn't Gyeol's Dad either.

48
00:03:17,128 --> 00:03:19,528
Well, this is a new one.

49
00:03:21,668 --> 00:03:24,428
I'll be sleeping on the floor, so I'll catch you if you fall.

50
00:03:24,698 --> 00:03:26,968
So toss and turn all you want. Just sleep comfortably.

51
00:03:27,038 --> 00:03:28,738
Yes, thank you.

52
00:03:29,308 --> 00:03:30,538
All right...

53
00:03:33,138 --> 00:03:35,078
Do you sleep well in unfamiliar places?

54
00:03:35,748 --> 00:03:36,878
No.

55
00:03:38,078 --> 00:03:40,078
Oh, what should I do then?

56
00:03:41,918 --> 00:03:43,018
When I was a kid,

57
00:03:43,148 --> 00:03:44,988
I always fell asleep when someone read me a storybook.

58
00:03:45,418 --> 00:03:49,128
- Did you bring a storybook? - No. I only have my workbooks.

59
00:03:49,688 --> 00:03:50,928
Want me to read your workbook?

60
00:03:52,828 --> 00:03:55,628
Right. This isn't the time to be reading a workbook,

61
00:03:55,698 --> 00:03:56,898
at bedtime.

62
00:03:58,368 --> 00:03:59,468
What should I do?

63
00:03:59,538 --> 00:04:01,138
Sing me a lullaby.

64
00:04:03,608 --> 00:04:07,378
- A lullaby? - Yes. When mom sings me a lullaby,

65
00:04:07,438 --> 00:04:10,808
- I fall right to sleep. - She's such a loving mom to you,

66
00:04:11,518 --> 00:04:13,318
so why do you make her so upset?

67
00:04:14,078 --> 00:04:15,318
I don't know.

68
00:04:15,518 --> 00:04:17,648
I just keep getting angry for some reason.

69
00:04:21,258 --> 00:04:23,758
It's because you love your mom so much.

70
00:04:29,568 --> 00:04:31,298
I can sing you a lullaby,

71
00:04:31,998 --> 00:04:34,068
but I'm not as good as your mom.

72
00:04:34,938 --> 00:04:36,208
Will that be okay?

73
00:04:37,768 --> 00:04:38,978
It's fine.

74
00:04:39,838 --> 00:04:40,838
Okay.

75
00:04:50,388 --> 00:04:55,358
Sleep well, little one

76
00:04:57,388 --> 00:05:02,268
In the front yard and on the back hill

77
00:05:04,268 --> 00:05:09,768
The birds and the little lambs

78
00:05:11,378 --> 00:05:16,808
Are all sleeping

79
00:05:19,078 --> 00:05:24,248
The moon through the window

80
00:05:26,188 --> 00:05:31,658
Sends silver and golden beads

81
00:05:34,098 --> 00:05:39,338
On this night

82
00:05:44,138 --> 00:05:49,778
Sleep well, my little one

83
00:06:05,298 --> 00:06:07,598
Are you hungry? Just a minute.

84
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:12,538
What are you doing?

85
00:06:13,568 --> 00:06:15,268
I sent my mom a text.

86
00:06:15,368 --> 00:06:18,638
- I'll stay at your place a while. - For a while?

87
00:06:19,278 --> 00:06:20,278
Longer?

88
00:06:21,208 --> 00:06:22,378
You want to keep staying here?

89
00:06:22,878 --> 00:06:24,178
Can't I?

90
00:06:25,548 --> 00:06:27,178
Can't you? Of course, you can.

91
00:06:27,918 --> 00:06:30,018
Of course, you can. Why wouldn't it be okay?

92
00:06:37,788 --> 00:06:40,958
Ma'am, until I'm done thinking,

93
00:06:41,528 --> 00:06:43,698
I'm going to stay at Mu Jin's for a while.

94
00:06:50,868 --> 00:06:52,208
Hey, I'm coming in.

95
00:07:02,418 --> 00:07:03,418
Gyu Oh.

96
00:07:03,488 --> 00:07:05,358
"Ma'am, until I'm done thinking,"

97
00:07:05,418 --> 00:07:07,718
"I'm going to stay at Mu Jin's for a while?"

98
00:07:10,758 --> 00:07:11,958
Give me the phone.

99
00:07:16,198 --> 00:07:17,828
Want me to go drag that punk back here?

100
00:07:18,398 --> 00:07:20,698
No, it's fine. He said he'll be back when he's done thinking.

101
00:07:20,768 --> 00:07:23,468
When is he going to be done thinking? The little brat.

102
00:07:23,768 --> 00:07:26,808
- Will he wait till mom wastes away? - Han Gyu Oh.

103
00:07:26,878 --> 00:07:29,178
I can't believe what a little punk he is.

104
00:07:29,848 --> 00:07:32,518
What kind of kid calls his own mom "Ma'am?"

105
00:07:33,318 --> 00:07:36,818
- I ought to just... Darn it. - You ought to just what?

106
00:07:38,388 --> 00:07:41,318
If words don't work, he needs to be disciplined.

107
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,458
Don't we have a switch in this house?

108
00:07:43,788 --> 00:07:45,058
Should I go get one?

109
00:07:45,558 --> 00:07:47,898
Han Gyu Oh, why are you the one overreacting?

110
00:07:48,128 --> 00:07:50,398
Why would you hit him?

111
00:07:51,438 --> 00:07:53,568
He's already going through so much. How dare you lay a hand on him?

112
00:07:53,938 --> 00:07:55,768
If you so much as lay a finger on Gyeol,

113
00:07:56,438 --> 00:07:59,538
- I will break your wrist first. - It is just upsetting...

114
00:07:59,608 --> 00:08:03,708
to see you losing your mind and struggling like this.

115
00:08:03,808 --> 00:08:06,178
Over some little brat. Darn it.

116
00:08:08,318 --> 00:08:11,318
You punk, you think you can get away with anything?

117
00:08:11,458 --> 00:08:13,558
What do you mean, "some little brat?"

118
00:08:16,758 --> 00:08:19,258
He's my child. What about it?

119
00:08:20,798 --> 00:08:23,328
He's my son, more precious than my own life.

120
00:08:23,498 --> 00:08:24,698
What about it?

121
00:08:25,238 --> 00:08:27,698
I would not trade him for 1,000 punks like you.

122
00:08:28,408 --> 00:08:29,638
He's my child.

123
00:08:30,338 --> 00:08:31,338
So what are you going to do about it?

124
00:08:32,208 --> 00:08:35,378
Okay, I get it. But let's be honest now.

125
00:08:35,908 --> 00:08:37,478
Gyeol is not your son, is he?

126
00:08:38,218 --> 00:08:39,948
You did not give birth to him, right?

127
00:08:40,748 --> 00:08:42,888
Why on earth did you raise a child that is not even yours?

128
00:08:43,048 --> 00:08:45,358
I mean, what were you thinking, raising him?

129
00:08:46,158 --> 00:08:48,458
Our father, Han Gyu Young, me, the twins.

130
00:08:49,058 --> 00:08:51,228
We were all obstacles standing in your way.

131
00:08:51,358 --> 00:08:52,898
Was not that enough for you?

132
00:09:02,868 --> 00:09:04,008
I...

133
00:09:05,178 --> 00:09:07,338
never begged you all for anything.

134
00:09:08,778 --> 00:09:10,448
I never asked you to carry Gyeol on your back,

135
00:09:11,448 --> 00:09:13,248
to make him a bottle,

136
00:09:15,018 --> 00:09:16,848
or to change his diaper.

137
00:09:17,818 --> 00:09:20,018
I never asked for your help, not even once.

138
00:09:21,858 --> 00:09:25,228
I raised Gyeol all by myself. All me.

139
00:09:26,128 --> 00:09:28,368
I carried him on my back to my part-time jobs...

140
00:09:29,228 --> 00:09:31,028
and I raised him myself.

141
00:09:32,898 --> 00:09:33,898
So,

142
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:36,138
shut your mouth.

143
00:09:38,178 --> 00:09:40,978
No one gets to say anything to me or to Gyeol.

144
00:09:41,508 --> 00:09:42,778
Do not say a word.

145
00:09:43,548 --> 00:09:45,218
All of you, just shut up.

146
00:09:47,848 --> 00:09:49,318
Do not even make a peep.

147
00:10:26,118 --> 00:10:28,328
Hold the twist.

148
00:10:28,388 --> 00:10:30,788
Stretch your left arm back and to the side...

149
00:10:31,158 --> 00:10:33,198
How can you possibly eat right now?

150
00:10:34,328 --> 00:10:37,598
If I get involved in that, the police would have to be called.

151
00:10:38,598 --> 00:10:41,498
Han Gyu Rim has turned into a total thug, I swear.

152
00:10:41,568 --> 00:10:43,238
Besides, that witch hit me yesterday,

153
00:10:43,308 --> 00:10:44,768
and I'm telling you, she almost broke my nose.

154
00:10:44,838 --> 00:10:47,438
You got hit too? Why?

155
00:10:49,248 --> 00:10:51,278
You must have deserved it.

156
00:10:52,078 --> 00:10:54,718
And did you deserve to get your ass kicked just now?

157
00:10:55,018 --> 00:10:57,848
I absolutely deserved it.

158
00:10:58,418 --> 00:11:00,018
I'm lucky she didn't kill me.

159
00:11:00,288 --> 00:11:01,358
What are you talking about?

160
00:11:02,128 --> 00:11:03,728
When someone says something bad about their own kid,

161
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:05,228
what parent wouldn't lose it?

162
00:11:06,758 --> 00:11:09,828
Hey, he's not her biological son.

163
00:11:10,328 --> 00:11:11,668
You said Gyu Rim didn't give birth to him.

164
00:11:14,568 --> 00:11:17,038
Why are you glaring at me?

165
00:11:17,108 --> 00:11:18,438
Hey, I was just repeating what you said.

166
00:11:18,508 --> 00:11:19,738
Why are you glaring at me like that?

167
00:11:20,808 --> 00:11:22,278
I have a question for you.

168
00:11:22,978 --> 00:11:24,478
What does a child mean to you, Father?

169
00:11:27,018 --> 00:11:29,448
Hey, why are you turning this on me now?

170
00:11:29,518 --> 00:11:32,418
Gosh. Do I look like a pushover to you?

171
00:11:32,588 --> 00:11:33,818
Darn it.

172
00:11:34,958 --> 00:11:37,688
Hey, pick one. Either you side with your sister...

173
00:11:37,758 --> 00:11:40,228
- or you fight her. - Exactly.

174
00:11:47,298 --> 00:11:49,738
Why are you all glaring at me now?

175
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:52,038
Hey, do I look like a pushover to you guys too?

176
00:11:52,478 --> 00:11:53,708
Why did you do it?

177
00:11:54,138 --> 00:11:55,348
Hey, do what?

178
00:11:55,948 --> 00:11:57,208
When Gyeol was little,

179
00:11:58,048 --> 00:12:00,278
even when he'd ask, "Grandpa, please play with me,"

180
00:12:00,348 --> 00:12:01,948
you never once gave him a ride on your bike,

181
00:12:02,088 --> 00:12:03,688
and you wouldn't let him call you Grandpa.

182
00:12:03,748 --> 00:12:06,558
You wouldn't even acknowledge him in public. Unbelievable.

183
00:12:06,618 --> 00:12:08,688
Hey, that's because I wasn't old enough...

184
00:12:08,758 --> 00:12:10,458
to be called Grandpa. All right?

185
00:12:10,758 --> 00:12:12,558
Gyeol kept calling me Grandpa, Grandpa, and...

186
00:12:12,928 --> 00:12:15,168
it made me feel like my life was over.

187
00:12:15,228 --> 00:12:17,028
If he can't call you Grandpa, should he call you Grandma?

188
00:12:17,668 --> 00:12:18,668
Should he have called you his brother?

189
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:20,838
Seriously, not letting him call his grandpa Grandpa.

190
00:12:21,238 --> 00:12:22,568
What is Gyeol, Hong Gil Dong?

191
00:12:22,868 --> 00:12:26,108
Hong Gil Dong couldn't call his father "Father."

192
00:12:27,808 --> 00:12:28,808
It could be on a test, so I wanted...

193
00:12:28,878 --> 00:12:29,908
to make sure you didn't get it wrong.

194
00:12:29,978 --> 00:12:31,108
Oh, you're so smart.

195
00:12:31,408 --> 00:12:33,618
Oh, for goodness' sake.

196
00:12:33,748 --> 00:12:36,488
Hey, wait until you all have kids of your own. Okay?

197
00:12:36,788 --> 00:12:38,518
My precious daughter, right?

198
00:12:38,688 --> 00:12:41,518
She has a baby by herself, unmarried and with no husband,

199
00:12:41,758 --> 00:12:43,488
and my child has her whole future ahead of her,

200
00:12:43,658 --> 00:12:44,888
but that little pea-sized kid...

201
00:12:44,958 --> 00:12:46,558
is blocking her path like a bulldozer.

202
00:12:48,158 --> 00:12:49,228
That little nuisance with no father?

203
00:12:50,328 --> 00:12:52,538
Why would he seem so precious and lovely to me?

204
00:12:52,698 --> 00:12:53,898
So people who can't get married...

205
00:12:53,968 --> 00:12:55,438
or don't have husbands can't have kids?

206
00:12:55,638 --> 00:12:59,108
Hey, who said they can't? They can.

207
00:12:59,808 --> 00:13:00,808
If she were on her own,

208
00:13:00,878 --> 00:13:02,048
she could have ten kids for all I care,

209
00:13:02,108 --> 00:13:05,478
but she shouldn't embarrass the family she lives with.

210
00:13:06,018 --> 00:13:08,218
I've never been embarrassed because of Gyu Rim or Gyeol.

211
00:13:08,788 --> 00:13:09,788
Me neither.

212
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:13,158
Like father, like children, right?

213
00:13:13,218 --> 00:13:15,288
People called us a broken family, ground up in a high-powered blender.

214
00:13:15,488 --> 00:13:17,758
You all lived with people pointing fingers...

215
00:13:17,828 --> 00:13:19,128
and whispering about us.

216
00:13:20,858 --> 00:13:22,698
Me again?

217
00:13:23,068 --> 00:13:25,468
Hey, am I the source of all your problems?

218
00:13:25,868 --> 00:13:26,868
Anyway, from now on,

219
00:13:26,938 --> 00:13:30,168
I won't let anyone who messes with Gyu Rim or Gyeol get away with it.

220
00:13:30,808 --> 00:13:32,778
What? Are you going to hit me too, then?

221
00:13:33,108 --> 00:13:35,708
Yes. If you deserve it, I will.

222
00:13:36,278 --> 00:13:37,448
So be careful from now on.

223
00:13:37,878 --> 00:13:40,248
- Han Gyu Seo, has he lost his mind? - Hey, enough!

224
00:13:40,318 --> 00:13:42,388
You'll have to get through me first.

225
00:13:42,948 --> 00:13:44,518
The people who mess with Gyu Rim and Gyeol...

226
00:13:44,588 --> 00:13:47,458
I'll crush them before Gyu Seo can. Just so you know.

227
00:13:48,188 --> 00:13:50,358
What's with these two? Seriously?

228
00:13:50,528 --> 00:13:52,458
I'm so scared. I don't know how I'll go on living.

229
00:13:52,858 --> 00:13:55,698
Father, why did you raise a bunch of gangsters?

230
00:13:55,968 --> 00:13:59,498
Oh, gosh. All right.

231
00:14:00,998 --> 00:14:04,138
It's all my fault. Everything, right? It's all my fault.

232
00:14:04,208 --> 00:14:05,678
Oh, gosh.

233
00:14:06,408 --> 00:14:08,478
Oh, man. Hey.

234
00:14:09,008 --> 00:14:11,378
If you all resent me this much,

235
00:14:11,478 --> 00:14:14,318
let's meet again in the next life, okay?

236
00:14:14,648 --> 00:14:17,918
Hey, in the next life, you can be the parents. All right?

237
00:14:18,558 --> 00:14:21,418
Hey, let's see if you can have and raise kids...

238
00:14:21,488 --> 00:14:22,588
however you want.

239
00:14:22,658 --> 00:14:23,788
Let's switch roles and see how you do.

240
00:14:23,858 --> 00:14:24,858
What do you say?

241
00:14:24,928 --> 00:14:26,558
- Are you crazy? - Why would I do that?

242
00:14:26,628 --> 00:14:27,628
- No! - No!

243
00:14:28,058 --> 00:14:31,028
Hey. Why do you have to say no in unison three times?

244
00:14:31,528 --> 00:14:32,538
- Do you hate me that much? - Yes.

245
00:14:35,068 --> 00:14:36,468
That girl.

246
00:14:37,638 --> 00:14:38,638
Why would we be happy about it?

247
00:14:42,108 --> 00:14:46,218
- My head... - What's this?

248
00:14:52,488 --> 00:14:54,458
What's wrong? Does it taste bad?

249
00:14:55,688 --> 00:14:57,628
No, it's delicious.

250
00:14:58,758 --> 00:15:01,868
But I don't really have an appetite.

251
00:15:03,228 --> 00:15:05,168
It's because you sent that text to your mom.

252
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:06,638
You're feeling bad about it.

253
00:15:07,338 --> 00:15:09,438
You might get an upset stomach, so chew your food well.

254
00:15:10,368 --> 00:15:11,468
Drink some juice too.

255
00:15:18,308 --> 00:15:21,378
Oh, what about the tall guy with the small eyes?

256
00:15:21,718 --> 00:15:24,118
Who? Oh, Jung Woo?

257
00:15:24,948 --> 00:15:26,788
He left early this morning in a huff.

258
00:15:29,858 --> 00:15:31,088
You should be careful too.

259
00:15:31,898 --> 00:15:33,758
Old habits die hard, you know.

260
00:15:34,328 --> 00:15:36,628
Hey, what are you going to do if you grow up to be like Jung Woo?

261
00:15:36,928 --> 00:15:39,038
He's so tall, but he's incredibly petty.

262
00:15:39,838 --> 00:15:41,098
I wasn't sulking.

263
00:15:41,598 --> 00:15:43,468
I was just being very honest.

264
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:44,768
Really?

265
00:15:45,578 --> 00:15:46,708
Honest. Okay.

266
00:15:47,378 --> 00:15:49,308
In that case, can I be honest with you too?

267
00:15:49,808 --> 00:15:50,808
Yes.

268
00:15:51,378 --> 00:15:52,878
You know I like your mom, right?

269
00:15:53,278 --> 00:15:54,278
Yes.

270
00:15:54,518 --> 00:15:57,648
When you're so harsh with your mom like that...

271
00:15:57,888 --> 00:15:59,558
I honestly don't like it at all.

272
00:16:00,618 --> 00:16:03,628
Then what am I supposed to do if I can't control my own feelings?

273
00:16:03,728 --> 00:16:05,358
Then you need to discipline your feelings.

274
00:16:05,528 --> 00:16:06,698
Tell them that's not allowed.

275
00:16:07,258 --> 00:16:10,268
You shouldn't act that way, especially not to your own mother.

276
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,898
Hey, to someone as kind and good as your mom...

277
00:16:12,968 --> 00:16:14,368
You of all people shouldn't do that to her. Seriously.

278
00:16:18,308 --> 00:16:20,208
You were in a lot of pain, weren't you, Gyu Oh?

279
00:16:21,278 --> 00:16:22,308
I'm sorry.

280
00:16:26,418 --> 00:16:28,148
(You were in a lot of pain, weren't you, Gyu Oh?)

281
00:16:39,828 --> 00:16:41,598
I'll do it. You should go inside.

282
00:16:42,328 --> 00:16:43,468
Don't you have school?

283
00:16:44,228 --> 00:16:45,298
Today's Saturday.

284
00:16:49,238 --> 00:16:51,708
I'm sorry about this morning. I caused a scene.

285
00:16:51,868 --> 00:16:53,708
Still, how could you slap him?

286
00:16:56,608 --> 00:16:58,408
How could you only slap one cheek?

287
00:16:58,948 --> 00:17:01,418
You should have just slapped both of them.

288
00:17:02,048 --> 00:17:03,818
So he'd be too scared to even make a peep from now on.

289
00:17:08,888 --> 00:17:11,828
Gosh, now your hand is all swollen for nothing.

290
00:17:13,498 --> 00:17:14,598
From now on, if you need to hit Han Gyu Oh,

291
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:15,668
tell me.

292
00:17:16,298 --> 00:17:18,198
My punch is 100 times stronger than Gyu Oh's.

293
00:17:20,838 --> 00:17:21,838
Do you also...

294
00:17:23,238 --> 00:17:24,538
miss Mom?

295
00:17:27,108 --> 00:17:29,708
How did you manage when you missed Mom, Gyu Seo?

296
00:17:31,678 --> 00:17:33,078
I never missed her.

297
00:17:34,278 --> 00:17:35,318
Besides, I had you.

298
00:17:35,988 --> 00:17:37,118
You're all I need.

299
00:17:39,388 --> 00:17:40,458
I mean it.

300
00:17:43,658 --> 00:17:47,528
I'll take care of this, so go study.

301
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:50,268
You can't end up uneducated like me, okay?

302
00:17:52,668 --> 00:17:53,768
Want to go get some ribs?

303
00:17:54,568 --> 00:17:55,608
I'll buy you some ribs.

304
00:17:56,068 --> 00:17:57,908
I have enough money to buy you ribs.

305
00:17:58,638 --> 00:18:00,678
I'm busy. Go on, get out of here.

306
00:18:01,638 --> 00:18:03,878
You have to eat to keep going, and you have to keep going to win.

307
00:18:04,808 --> 00:18:06,348
If you use up all your energy,

308
00:18:06,518 --> 00:18:08,718
how will you have the strength to hug Gyeol when he gets here?

309
00:18:09,288 --> 00:18:10,348
That little guy.

310
00:18:10,718 --> 00:18:13,788
You have to hug him so tight you could pop him.

311
00:18:14,588 --> 00:18:17,758
So let's go get some ribs. I'll let Grandma know.

312
00:18:18,328 --> 00:18:19,628
Fine. Later.

313
00:18:20,028 --> 00:18:22,028
Let go of me. People are watching.

314
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:24,398
I'm not letting go until you say you'll go get ribs with me.

315
00:18:25,468 --> 00:18:27,238
I know this amazing rib place that's super famous.

316
00:18:27,368 --> 00:18:30,938
Why so stubborn? I'm so busy today.

317
00:18:31,608 --> 00:18:33,438
Then I'll help you with everything after we get ribs.

318
00:18:33,808 --> 00:18:35,578
I'm good at peeling onions and slicing radishes.

319
00:18:35,848 --> 00:18:37,348
- Fine, let go. - I'm sorry.

320
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:39,218
Let go and talk, Han Gyu Seo. You're hurting me.

321
00:18:39,218 --> 00:18:41,648
- I messed up. - Gyu Seo, let go.

322
00:18:56,568 --> 00:18:57,598
What are you doing?

323
00:18:58,068 --> 00:18:59,068
Quiet.

324
00:18:59,698 --> 00:19:01,668
You'll jinx it. Don't say a word.

325
00:19:05,308 --> 00:19:07,038
What did some shaman tell you this time?

326
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:09,678
Unbelievable.

327
00:19:10,308 --> 00:19:12,948
I told you to stop doing these pointless things.

328
00:19:14,078 --> 00:19:15,388
You rotten kid. Honestly.

329
00:19:15,888 --> 00:19:17,288
Do you have any idea how desperate I was...

330
00:19:17,348 --> 00:19:18,348
to resort to this?

331
00:19:19,318 --> 00:19:22,128
Do you know how much of the family savings you blew?

332
00:19:22,228 --> 00:19:24,188
The money? I'll pay it back.

333
00:19:24,688 --> 00:19:26,898
Oh, for goodness' sake.

334
00:19:27,858 --> 00:19:29,198
What nonsense.

335
00:19:29,268 --> 00:19:31,028
You're talking absolute nonsense.

336
00:19:35,968 --> 00:19:37,568
Here, take this.

337
00:19:38,878 --> 00:19:39,878
Oh my.

338
00:19:43,108 --> 00:19:45,448
Why does this feel so light?

339
00:19:46,378 --> 00:19:48,348
Don't tell me you thought all that money...

340
00:19:48,418 --> 00:19:49,788
was just 50 dollars?

341
00:19:56,128 --> 00:19:59,798
Let's see, 10, 100, 1,000, 10,000, 100,000 dollars?

342
00:20:00,228 --> 00:20:03,398
That includes the cancellation fees for the wedding and honeymoon,

343
00:20:03,598 --> 00:20:05,668
plus the settlement money you paid to get me out, right?

344
00:20:05,768 --> 00:20:06,768
Oh my goodness.

345
00:20:07,268 --> 00:20:10,008
But where did you get all this money?

346
00:20:10,068 --> 00:20:14,078
It's money I saved by not spending a thing. Okay?

347
00:20:15,108 --> 00:20:17,408
I worked as a designated driver, delivered packages,

348
00:20:17,578 --> 00:20:18,778
hauled bricks,

349
00:20:19,318 --> 00:20:21,678
caught shrimp, crawfish, whales.

350
00:20:21,948 --> 00:20:25,248
Well, not whales. But anyway.

351
00:20:27,888 --> 00:20:31,088
It's not a forged check. Can't you trust your own son?

352
00:20:39,798 --> 00:20:41,438
I'm so proud of you, my son.

353
00:20:42,438 --> 00:20:45,468
How did you save all this money?

354
00:20:45,838 --> 00:20:47,438
That's right.

355
00:20:48,338 --> 00:20:50,778
What does it matter what you did for it? Right.

356
00:20:51,708 --> 00:20:54,448
You earned it like a dog so you could spend it like a king.

357
00:20:54,918 --> 00:20:56,718
There's no such thing as a lowly job.

358
00:20:57,848 --> 00:21:00,958
You did a darn good job. Didn't you?

359
00:21:01,288 --> 00:21:04,788
Right? I knew you'd be proud of me.

360
00:21:05,698 --> 00:21:09,098
Proud of you? Don't make me laugh, you rotten kid.

361
00:21:10,028 --> 00:21:13,938
You throw away all this money you bled for in one go?

362
00:21:14,498 --> 00:21:15,538
You rotten kid.

363
00:21:15,968 --> 00:21:17,568
All because you couldn't control your fists one time,

364
00:21:17,638 --> 00:21:20,208
look at the disaster you've caused.

365
00:21:20,578 --> 00:21:22,808
And you're not even bothered by this?

366
00:21:23,408 --> 00:21:25,208
When I look at this money again,

367
00:21:25,378 --> 00:21:26,618
my stomach, that I thought dissolved from shock,

368
00:21:26,678 --> 00:21:28,988
is starting to churn all over again.

369
00:21:29,388 --> 00:21:30,748
Look, anyway...

370
00:21:31,118 --> 00:21:34,088
We're all settled up. Whatever the shaman said,

371
00:21:34,158 --> 00:21:37,658
whatever the psychic said, don't say any of that to me anymore.

372
00:21:41,098 --> 00:21:43,598
Fine, we'll only listen to your precious fortune-teller then.

373
00:21:43,668 --> 00:21:45,328
- Mom. - Honestly.

374
00:21:46,198 --> 00:21:49,238
In the very back of a drawer in your room,

375
00:21:49,808 --> 00:21:54,138
I found a camera. So I smashed it.

376
00:21:56,248 --> 00:21:58,808
Oh, really? Good for you...

377
00:21:58,948 --> 00:22:03,688
- You did a great job smashing it. - But why was the camera there?

378
00:22:04,088 --> 00:22:07,458
Didn't I tell you to stay away from cameras? Did I or not?

379
00:22:07,518 --> 00:22:08,618
Well...

380
00:22:08,688 --> 00:22:10,288
Why was that in there?

381
00:22:10,728 --> 00:22:12,728
I try to avoid anything that starts with "cam."

382
00:22:12,798 --> 00:22:13,928
I won't even go camping.

383
00:22:13,998 --> 00:22:15,668
Are you trying to be the death of me?

384
00:22:15,728 --> 00:22:18,828
You rotten brat. If you go near a camera one more time, that's it.

385
00:22:18,898 --> 00:22:20,668
I'll disown you, I swear.

386
00:22:20,738 --> 00:22:23,008
- You rotten child. - I don't know. It's not even mine.

387
00:22:23,068 --> 00:22:24,968
- You don't know? You brat. - I don't know.

388
00:22:25,038 --> 00:22:26,538
Then who put it there? Who?

389
00:22:26,608 --> 00:22:27,778
Did a thief put it there for you, you brat?

390
00:22:27,838 --> 00:22:28,838
I don't know.

391
00:22:50,798 --> 00:22:52,668
Okay. Let's take a ten minute break.

392
00:23:01,708 --> 00:23:04,908
Hey, there's our star artist.

393
00:23:04,978 --> 00:23:08,148
Hey, you jerk, let go. I'm not in the mood to fool around.

394
00:23:09,318 --> 00:23:10,318
Why's that? Why?

395
00:23:10,418 --> 00:23:11,688
Did something happen?

396
00:23:12,658 --> 00:23:14,088
The more I talk about it, the worse I'll feel,

397
00:23:14,158 --> 00:23:15,188
so just drop it.

398
00:23:15,618 --> 00:23:17,188
So, anything happen at the company?

399
00:23:18,288 --> 00:23:20,128
Anything happen? A lot has happened.

400
00:23:20,758 --> 00:23:23,568
They want to collaborate with us. You know?

401
00:23:23,668 --> 00:23:27,538
Seoksam Corporation, Jewang Textiles, Duseom, GL Fashion,

402
00:23:27,598 --> 00:23:31,738
from huge companies you'd recognize by name to all the smaller ones.

403
00:23:32,008 --> 00:23:34,108
- Let me see. - It's insane, Artist.

404
00:23:34,178 --> 00:23:36,578
I think we're about to hit it super, super big.

405
00:23:37,248 --> 00:23:41,118
And yesterday, a director from Ring Bio came...

406
00:23:41,178 --> 00:23:43,388
and said she wouldn't leave until she met you.

407
00:23:43,448 --> 00:23:44,448
She even ordered noodles...

408
00:23:44,518 --> 00:23:46,088
and ate them in front of your office.

409
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:48,858
She seems a little eccentric.

410
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:51,088
I got the business proposal...

411
00:23:51,158 --> 00:23:52,828
and the mood board from her.

412
00:23:53,628 --> 00:23:55,628
The whole vibe felt pretty good.

413
00:23:56,298 --> 00:23:58,868
Is that right? Let me see that mood board.

414
00:24:14,248 --> 00:24:15,248
What?

415
00:24:18,688 --> 00:24:20,858
Wow, this is impressive.

416
00:24:24,828 --> 00:24:27,528
Hey. Set up a meeting with this company.

417
00:24:28,428 --> 00:24:29,428
This director...

418
00:24:29,498 --> 00:24:31,298
She's extremely impatient.

419
00:24:31,628 --> 00:24:33,398
If you ask to see her, she'll come running right now.

420
00:24:33,568 --> 00:24:36,668
- Then tell her to come right now. - Really?

421
00:24:37,608 --> 00:24:38,738
Okay.

422
00:24:52,788 --> 00:24:55,158
You're Director Kim Yoon Jin from Ring Bio?

423
00:24:57,858 --> 00:24:59,898
You must be the artist Joel, correct?

424
00:25:00,298 --> 00:25:01,298
Yes.

425
00:25:02,358 --> 00:25:03,668
It's a pleasure to meet you.

426
00:25:05,328 --> 00:25:06,638
I'm Kim Yoon Jin.

427
00:25:08,068 --> 00:25:09,668
So, I heard that to meet me,

428
00:25:09,738 --> 00:25:11,808
you even ordered and ate noodles?

429
00:25:12,238 --> 00:25:13,238
Yes.

430
00:25:13,438 --> 00:25:15,578
The jajangmyeon there is actually quite delicious.

431
00:25:15,638 --> 00:25:17,848
I'm sorry to have put you through so much trouble.

432
00:25:18,108 --> 00:25:19,218
I have a bit of wanderlust,

433
00:25:19,278 --> 00:25:21,818
so I can't really stay cooped up in an office.

434
00:25:23,048 --> 00:25:25,188
I guess I was really lucky then.

435
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:45,408
Excellent. Let's work together.

436
00:25:46,508 --> 00:25:51,378
Right here? You're deciding just like that?

437
00:25:51,878 --> 00:25:54,718
Yes. I run a small-time operation.

438
00:25:54,778 --> 00:25:56,148
When dealing with the great Dongyoon,

439
00:25:56,218 --> 00:25:57,918
how can I afford to be picky?

440
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:00,988
Gosh...

441
00:26:01,618 --> 00:26:03,758
It was so hard to get a meeting with you,

442
00:26:03,828 --> 00:26:06,758
so I thought you'd be very difficult and particular.

443
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:09,968
Are you really okay with deciding this quickly?

444
00:26:10,298 --> 00:26:11,298
Yes.

445
00:26:12,738 --> 00:26:15,938
As for the other details and the future schedule,

446
00:26:16,008 --> 00:26:17,808
you can discuss them with my manager.

447
00:26:19,338 --> 00:26:22,308
Our business here is done, so I'll be going now.

448
00:26:24,248 --> 00:26:25,248
Right.

449
00:26:33,958 --> 00:26:36,428
I can't believe I found someone more impatient than me.

450
00:26:43,928 --> 00:26:45,598
Oh, honestly...

451
00:26:59,048 --> 00:27:00,848
Good grief, what's she doing sitting over there?

452
00:27:00,918 --> 00:27:01,948
Gosh, she gave me a scare.

453
00:27:02,818 --> 00:27:04,118
He's wearing that.

454
00:27:04,218 --> 00:27:06,718
I saw that at a fashion show in Paris earlier this year.

455
00:27:06,788 --> 00:27:08,158
Don't change the subject.

456
00:27:09,118 --> 00:27:10,288
So?

457
00:27:11,458 --> 00:27:13,298
What are you going to do?

458
00:27:15,158 --> 00:27:16,668
This marriage.

459
00:27:17,628 --> 00:27:18,998
Are you calling it off?

460
00:27:21,068 --> 00:27:22,568
I just came from the community service center...

461
00:27:22,638 --> 00:27:23,708
where I registered our marriage.

462
00:27:24,468 --> 00:27:26,738
Sung Wook just stamped the papers, and I went alone.

463
00:27:27,778 --> 00:27:29,878
You registered the marriage?

464
00:27:29,978 --> 00:27:30,978
Yes.

465
00:27:31,048 --> 00:27:32,878
Sung Wook and I are husband and wife now,

466
00:27:32,948 --> 00:27:34,548
and I am now your daughter-in-law.

467
00:27:36,288 --> 00:27:38,948
I hope we get along. I hope you'll welcome me.

468
00:27:39,088 --> 00:27:40,088
So then...

469
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:42,558
you've forgiven my Sung Wook?

470
00:27:42,828 --> 00:27:45,658
No. I haven't forgiven him yet,

471
00:27:45,728 --> 00:27:48,228
but I love him too much to just break up with him.

472
00:27:48,428 --> 00:27:49,728
I wanted to make him mine as soon as possible...

473
00:27:49,798 --> 00:27:53,298
- and rebuild him to be good as new. - Oh my goodness.

474
00:27:53,368 --> 00:27:57,408
My dear Gyu Young. You are so incredible.

475
00:27:58,108 --> 00:27:59,308
Then what about the wedding ceremony?

476
00:27:59,408 --> 00:28:02,338
- What about the wedding ceremony? - We're not going to have one.

477
00:28:03,048 --> 00:28:04,148
As for the wedding costs,

478
00:28:04,248 --> 00:28:06,718
we'll tell everyone we donated the money to the underprivileged.

479
00:28:06,918 --> 00:28:09,788
- Just go along with that, please. - My, my.

480
00:28:09,888 --> 00:28:14,588
How on earth did your parents raise such a brilliant daughter?

481
00:28:16,358 --> 00:28:19,428
Tell me, do your parents know what my Sung Wook did?

482
00:28:20,158 --> 00:28:21,858
It would be a disaster if they found out.

483
00:28:22,158 --> 00:28:24,768
I just told them we're skipping the wedding and honeymoon...

484
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:25,828
and that we're practicing...

485
00:28:25,898 --> 00:28:27,268
noblesse oblige with the money instead.

486
00:28:27,368 --> 00:28:28,498
That's all I said.

487
00:28:30,638 --> 00:28:33,238
I've really hit the daughter-in-law jackpot in my old age.

488
00:28:34,508 --> 00:28:35,508
Here.

489
00:28:35,778 --> 00:28:37,478
Let me see your hand.

490
00:28:41,048 --> 00:28:43,388
It's five carats.

491
00:28:44,148 --> 00:28:45,748
It's from a major brand.

492
00:28:46,088 --> 00:28:47,088
You have it.

493
00:28:47,788 --> 00:28:50,558
Oh, my. How could I possibly wear something so expensive?

494
00:28:52,728 --> 00:28:53,758
Take this...

495
00:28:53,828 --> 00:28:55,628
and please forgive my Sung Wook.

496
00:28:56,398 --> 00:28:59,668
He's not normally like this. Some little vixen seduced him,

497
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:02,098
and he just lost his mind for a moment.

498
00:29:02,268 --> 00:29:03,908
I know he's my son,

499
00:29:04,008 --> 00:29:06,608
but he's so pure and transparent...

500
00:29:08,508 --> 00:29:11,948
As innocent as a blank canvas. Oh, I don't feel so good.

501
00:29:12,408 --> 00:29:13,448
My stomach...

502
00:29:15,218 --> 00:29:16,488
Excuse me.

503
00:29:17,018 --> 00:29:18,518
I just need the restroom for a moment.

504
00:29:19,288 --> 00:29:20,288
Oh, my goodness...

505
00:29:20,788 --> 00:29:22,088
Please, go ahead.

506
00:29:22,188 --> 00:29:23,228
Okay.

507
00:29:28,558 --> 00:29:31,068
Next time, give me a house, Ma'am. A building, too.

508
00:29:31,128 --> 00:29:34,298
Give me a golf membership, some land, and a villa, please.

509
00:29:34,468 --> 00:29:36,338
I'll play the part of the vixen down to a T,

510
00:29:36,408 --> 00:29:38,468
so just give it all to me.

511
00:29:44,308 --> 00:29:45,648
My precious.

512
00:29:59,158 --> 00:30:02,098
When can I expect the money you promised me?

513
00:30:02,558 --> 00:30:04,768
Ji Yeol's surgery is coming up.

514
00:30:05,128 --> 00:30:07,868
It's very difficult for me to keep bringing this up.

515
00:30:08,538 --> 00:30:10,908
Please resolve this as soon as possible.

516
00:30:34,358 --> 00:30:35,658
You said you have no family, right?

517
00:30:43,038 --> 00:30:46,068
For the rest of your life, I will take care of you.

518
00:30:46,978 --> 00:30:48,608
Until I can put everything back the way it was.

519
00:31:05,128 --> 00:31:07,258
I just got cash from the bank.

520
00:31:07,958 --> 00:31:09,398
I'm going to buy you, Han Gyu Oh.

521
00:31:10,198 --> 00:31:11,728
Where do I go and how do I do it?

522
00:31:13,498 --> 00:31:14,498
She's insane.

523
00:31:20,638 --> 00:31:21,638
You don't recognize me?

524
00:31:22,338 --> 00:31:23,348
Han Gyu Oh.

525
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:24,648
You really don't remember?

526
00:31:25,778 --> 00:31:26,778
I don't.

527
00:31:27,278 --> 00:31:28,478
I've erased all my memories of it.

528
00:31:29,448 --> 00:31:30,518
So...

529
00:31:31,118 --> 00:31:32,118
Gyeol's Uncle,

530
00:31:32,188 --> 00:31:33,188
please pretend you don't know me either...

531
00:31:33,588 --> 00:31:34,918
if we ever happen to meet again.

532
00:32:11,488 --> 00:32:13,498
I was so scared you were going to call me a psycho...

533
00:32:13,558 --> 00:32:14,558
and then ghost me.

534
00:32:16,128 --> 00:32:17,168
So which hotel should we go to?

535
00:32:18,068 --> 00:32:19,098
The one you always go to...

536
00:32:21,498 --> 00:32:24,338
Since you're the one paying, you can book whichever one you like.

537
00:32:26,408 --> 00:32:28,978
Let's just catch our breath. What's the big rush?

538
00:32:35,048 --> 00:32:36,988
What I want from you is to date.

539
00:32:37,148 --> 00:32:38,318
A sweet, romantic relationship.

540
00:32:39,018 --> 00:32:41,188
The kind of relationship where I can tell everyone...

541
00:32:41,458 --> 00:32:43,028
that a great guy like you is my boyfriend.

542
00:32:44,958 --> 00:32:46,088
I'm not going to date you.

543
00:32:48,458 --> 00:32:49,768
But I'm the one with the money.

544
00:32:51,368 --> 00:32:53,738
And what I want to buy isn't your body, it's your soul.

545
00:32:57,768 --> 00:32:59,708
And you can wipe that sour look off your face.

546
00:33:01,208 --> 00:33:03,808
You don't have to make it so obvious that you're only here for the money.

547
00:33:04,208 --> 00:33:05,648
It hurts the feelings of the person paying.

548
00:33:09,648 --> 00:33:10,648
Fine.

549
00:33:11,218 --> 00:33:13,218
You can use me however you want.

550
00:33:13,818 --> 00:33:14,988
But let me tell you this upfront...

551
00:33:15,958 --> 00:33:17,958
I will never have feelings for you.

552
00:33:19,258 --> 00:33:20,328
Don't say that upfront.

553
00:33:20,928 --> 00:33:22,028
You never know what might happen.

554
00:33:22,968 --> 00:33:24,198
Let me tell you this upfront...

555
00:33:24,898 --> 00:33:26,398
you're exactly the type of person I can't stand.

556
00:33:39,618 --> 00:33:41,678
My man. Day one starts today.

557
00:33:46,488 --> 00:33:47,658
I knew you'd call.

558
00:33:48,088 --> 00:33:49,828
- It's been a while. - What's with your profile picture?

559
00:33:49,888 --> 00:33:51,458
Did you really decide to start dating Han Gyu Oh?

560
00:33:52,728 --> 00:33:54,558
We didn't just decide to date. We are dating.

561
00:33:55,198 --> 00:33:56,868
You're a teacher. Can't you even read?

562
00:33:58,098 --> 00:33:59,098
Day one starts today.

563
00:33:59,528 --> 00:34:00,638
You must be crazy.

564
00:34:02,398 --> 00:34:05,168
You can't be sane and in love.

565
00:34:06,378 --> 00:34:07,808
Are you with Han Gyu Oh right now?

566
00:34:08,078 --> 00:34:09,538
Of course. My boyfriend can't stand...

567
00:34:09,608 --> 00:34:11,178
to be away from me for even a second.

568
00:34:12,048 --> 00:34:13,048
Where are you?

569
00:34:13,548 --> 00:34:15,748
Why? Do you think I'm lying?

570
00:34:15,918 --> 00:34:17,148
Where are you?

571
00:34:32,268 --> 00:34:33,268
Why are you lying?

572
00:34:36,368 --> 00:34:37,368
I'm not lying.

573
00:34:38,308 --> 00:34:39,538
He just stepped out to take a call.

574
00:34:41,138 --> 00:34:43,608
Oh, and I didn't tell Han Gyu Oh you were coming.

575
00:34:45,378 --> 00:34:47,518
So, how can I prove it to you once and for all?

576
00:34:49,278 --> 00:34:51,018
Should I kiss him right in front of you?

577
00:34:55,258 --> 00:34:57,328
- Hey! - You piece of trash.

578
00:35:09,238 --> 00:35:12,168
Babe. This girl must be insane.

579
00:35:18,308 --> 00:35:20,678
Where are you going? Han Gyu Oh!

580
00:35:20,948 --> 00:35:22,478
Hey, where do you think you're going, you jerk.

581
00:35:33,628 --> 00:35:35,398
Hey, you're a little kid.

582
00:35:35,458 --> 00:35:36,468
Why do you want to come see the river...

583
00:35:37,498 --> 00:35:39,028
and not an amusement park?

584
00:35:39,568 --> 00:35:43,068
When I came here with you last time, I really liked it.

585
00:35:46,308 --> 00:35:48,078
We really do have a lot in common.

586
00:35:49,138 --> 00:35:50,148
Right?

587
00:35:51,678 --> 00:35:53,678
- Mister. - Yes?

588
00:35:54,678 --> 00:35:55,678
By any chance...

589
00:35:56,988 --> 00:35:58,218
are you my dad?

590
00:36:03,458 --> 00:36:04,458
No.

591
00:36:21,338 --> 00:36:22,678
What are you thinking about?

592
00:36:24,678 --> 00:36:25,848
The same thing as you.

593
00:36:28,648 --> 00:36:30,888
You were thinking about my mom?

594
00:36:32,318 --> 00:36:34,018
Why? Can't I?

595
00:36:35,258 --> 00:36:37,958
So you really do like my mom.

596
00:36:42,758 --> 00:36:44,428
How long have you liked her?

597
00:36:44,868 --> 00:36:46,168
Since before you were born.

598
00:36:47,468 --> 00:36:50,768
You've liked her this whole time? Since before I was born?

599
00:36:51,638 --> 00:36:52,638
It's a secret, kid.

600
00:36:53,538 --> 00:36:55,008
That's not fair.

601
00:36:55,308 --> 00:36:58,678
I told you everything with complete honesty.

602
00:37:02,948 --> 00:37:05,748
I'll keep it a secret. Man to man.

603
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:23,138
From the day I first met her nine years ago until now.

604
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:28,308
Not for a single minute...

605
00:37:29,178 --> 00:37:30,648
Have I ever stopped liking her.

606
00:37:37,518 --> 00:37:38,518
What?

607
00:37:41,218 --> 00:37:42,218
Am I being cheesy?

608
00:37:43,658 --> 00:37:44,658
Gosh.

609
00:37:46,088 --> 00:37:48,428
I can't believe the things I'm telling you.

610
00:37:49,128 --> 00:37:50,298
Get up. Let's go home.

611
00:37:51,228 --> 00:37:52,468
We're leaving now?

612
00:37:53,838 --> 00:37:56,398
If we keep talking, I feel like I'll tell you everything.

613
00:37:56,968 --> 00:38:00,108
I'm hungry too. I'll make you some carbonara pasta.

614
00:38:00,178 --> 00:38:02,608
Not carbonara, I want seafood tomato.

615
00:38:03,308 --> 00:38:06,048
All right, I'll make you seafood tomato pasta. Let's go.

616
00:38:16,758 --> 00:38:17,758
Why aren't you answering?

617
00:38:17,988 --> 00:38:20,198
I can't answer it yet.

618
00:38:20,928 --> 00:38:22,498
Your mom will worry if you don't answer.

619
00:38:24,098 --> 00:38:27,698
Can you answer it for me and tell her Gyeol is doing fine?

620
00:38:28,938 --> 00:38:29,938
Gyeol.

621
00:38:30,308 --> 00:38:31,768
I have to use the restroom.

622
00:38:38,808 --> 00:38:41,018
(Mom)

623
00:38:43,488 --> 00:38:44,718
Gyeol, it's Mom.

624
00:38:45,388 --> 00:38:47,218
Thank you for answering my call.

625
00:38:47,558 --> 00:38:48,758
Thank you so much, Gyeol.

626
00:38:50,288 --> 00:38:53,498
I just called because I miss you.

627
00:38:54,658 --> 00:38:56,598
If you don't feel like talking yet, you don't have to.

628
00:38:56,698 --> 00:38:57,798
I'll do all the talking.

629
00:38:58,598 --> 00:38:59,828
Gyeol, have you eaten?

630
00:39:00,998 --> 00:39:01,998
What did you eat?

631
00:39:03,308 --> 00:39:04,938
Did the mister make you something tasty?

632
00:39:05,668 --> 00:39:06,678
What about sleep?

633
00:39:07,238 --> 00:39:09,508
You can't sleep without your favorite pillow.

634
00:39:09,948 --> 00:39:11,078
Did you sleep well?

635
00:39:12,908 --> 00:39:13,978
Gyeol, I'm sorry.

636
00:39:14,548 --> 00:39:15,718
I said you didn't have to talk,

637
00:39:15,818 --> 00:39:17,588
but then all I did was ask questions, right?

638
00:39:19,818 --> 00:39:20,818
I'm sorry.

639
00:39:21,958 --> 00:39:23,328
I'm so sorry, Gyeol.

640
00:39:28,258 --> 00:39:30,898
Gyeol had to use the restroom, so he just stepped out.

641
00:39:33,438 --> 00:39:36,138
He's eating well,

642
00:39:36,808 --> 00:39:38,138
sleeping well, and he's regular.

643
00:39:39,708 --> 00:39:40,838
He's doing better than you'd think.

644
00:39:42,538 --> 00:39:44,608
He had a rice omelet for breakfast,

645
00:39:45,578 --> 00:39:47,248
and for lunch, we went out...

646
00:39:48,118 --> 00:39:49,748
and had spicy stir-fried chicken and buckwheat noodles.

647
00:39:50,818 --> 00:39:54,018
For dinner, he said he wanted seafood tomato pasta,

648
00:39:54,088 --> 00:39:55,088
so I'm planning to make that.

649
00:39:58,188 --> 00:39:59,558
Oh, and about his favorite pillow?

650
00:39:59,658 --> 00:40:02,458
He had a little trouble sleeping at first without it.

651
00:40:06,298 --> 00:40:07,698
But I sang him a lullaby,

652
00:40:08,798 --> 00:40:10,638
and he was fast asleep in 20 minutes.

653
00:40:10,968 --> 00:40:13,238
Other than getting up to pee at three in the morning,

654
00:40:14,208 --> 00:40:16,378
he slept soundly until eight without waking up once.

655
00:40:18,178 --> 00:40:20,848
But since he didn't bring anything besides his toothbrush,

656
00:40:21,178 --> 00:40:23,148
I was wondering if I should go to a department store.

657
00:40:23,818 --> 00:40:25,248
A change of clothes,

658
00:40:25,748 --> 00:40:27,618
underwear, socks, and pajamas.

659
00:40:29,158 --> 00:40:30,188
What else is there?

660
00:40:31,458 --> 00:40:34,358
A kids' spoon and bowl, a storybook.

661
00:40:36,328 --> 00:40:37,328
What else?

662
00:40:38,928 --> 00:40:40,298
Anyway, I'm going to swing by your place later,

663
00:40:40,368 --> 00:40:41,438
so could you pack those things for me?

664
00:40:52,608 --> 00:40:54,778
We're going to stop by your mom's on the way home.

665
00:40:56,448 --> 00:40:58,288
You can't go to school wearing my clothes, right?

666
00:40:59,448 --> 00:41:01,358
Want to try? I'm kind of curious.

667
00:41:01,858 --> 00:41:02,858
No.

668
00:41:03,958 --> 00:41:07,558
A change of clothes, your pajamas, underwear, socks,

669
00:41:08,728 --> 00:41:11,198
and that favorite pillow of yours? I asked her to pack them.

670
00:41:13,468 --> 00:41:14,468
Okay.

671
00:41:53,578 --> 00:41:54,938
Gyeol fell asleep a little while ago.

672
00:41:57,008 --> 00:41:58,048
I'll take it.

673
00:42:00,778 --> 00:42:01,848
This is Gyeol's step stool...

674
00:42:01,918 --> 00:42:04,518
for when he brushes his teeth and washes his face.

675
00:42:06,248 --> 00:42:07,258
Right.

676
00:42:36,748 --> 00:42:37,818
Should I wake Gyeol up?

677
00:42:39,548 --> 00:42:40,558
No.

678
00:42:43,458 --> 00:42:46,858
You can't even work because of him. I feel so terrible.

679
00:42:48,058 --> 00:42:49,058
It's all right.

680
00:42:49,458 --> 00:42:51,168
I only ever see that gloomy kid, Jung Woo,

681
00:42:51,468 --> 00:42:54,068
so thanks to Gyeol, I'm not bored and it's actually fun.

682
00:42:58,168 --> 00:42:59,168
I'll get going.

683
00:43:01,408 --> 00:43:02,408
Thank you.

684
00:43:03,548 --> 00:43:04,548
Go on.

685
00:43:14,588 --> 00:43:15,658
The truth...

686
00:43:17,228 --> 00:43:20,428
Being honest may not always be the right thing,

687
00:43:21,828 --> 00:43:24,868
and it might hurt someone or even be cruel,

688
00:43:26,598 --> 00:43:28,798
but I think it's better than lying and avoiding it.

689
00:43:32,138 --> 00:43:33,168
Don't be afraid.

690
00:43:39,748 --> 00:43:41,548
If you get too scared, you can always talk to me,

691
00:43:42,248 --> 00:43:43,518
and I'll do my best to help.

692
00:43:49,288 --> 00:43:50,288
I'm really going now.

693
00:44:10,778 --> 00:44:12,348
(Min Ju)

694
00:44:24,088 --> 00:44:25,888
(Suh Min Ju)

695
00:44:35,768 --> 00:44:36,898
Okay, let's talk now.

696
00:44:39,238 --> 00:44:40,238
Go ahead.

697
00:44:41,478 --> 00:44:43,948
Can you please explain this ridiculous situation to me?

698
00:44:45,348 --> 00:44:47,048
I think you're the one who needs to do the explaining.

699
00:44:52,488 --> 00:44:56,018
How could you be dating Suh Min Ju? Don't you know who she is?

700
00:44:56,358 --> 00:44:58,228
She's your friend Su Chan's girlfriend...

701
00:44:58,288 --> 00:44:59,788
and my best friend, Suh Min Ju.

702
00:45:01,858 --> 00:45:02,858
So?

703
00:45:03,768 --> 00:45:04,768
So?

704
00:45:05,898 --> 00:45:07,538
You said you erased me from your memory.

705
00:45:08,238 --> 00:45:10,098
You said we should live as strangers.

706
00:45:10,938 --> 00:45:13,268
So why should you care who I date?

707
00:45:14,608 --> 00:45:17,048
You don't want me, but you don't want...

708
00:45:17,108 --> 00:45:18,608
anyone else to have me.

709
00:45:19,248 --> 00:45:20,248
Is that why you did it?

710
00:45:21,118 --> 00:45:24,088
Is that why you made that cringey scene with the coffee?

711
00:45:24,648 --> 00:45:26,018
Are you that desperate for a woman?

712
00:45:26,548 --> 00:45:27,618
Can't you live without one?

713
00:45:28,118 --> 00:45:29,918
Even if there wasn't another woman in the world,

714
00:45:30,118 --> 00:45:31,858
why Min Ju? Seriously?

715
00:45:32,588 --> 00:45:33,698
Are you lonely or something?

716
00:45:34,358 --> 00:45:37,368
You might as well ask out a random woman on the street then.

717
00:45:38,468 --> 00:45:39,468
Should I?

718
00:45:39,928 --> 00:45:41,898
- Should you? - I'll consider it.

719
00:45:45,868 --> 00:45:48,808
So stop worrying about who I see...

720
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:52,178
and let's just stop playing these games.

721
00:45:56,548 --> 00:45:57,548
Hey!

722
00:45:57,618 --> 00:45:59,318
Don't you even feel bad for Su Chan?

723
00:45:59,688 --> 00:46:01,218
Is that all your friendship amounts to?

724
00:46:01,718 --> 00:46:02,788
Are you a scumbag?

725
00:46:03,358 --> 00:46:04,558
Yes, I'm a scumbag.

726
00:46:05,728 --> 00:46:07,528
I don't care if it's Min Ju or anyone else.

727
00:46:07,598 --> 00:46:09,458
- Hey, Han Gyu Oh. - If it's not Kwon Hee Na,

728
00:46:11,528 --> 00:46:12,798
I don't care who it is.

729
00:46:14,698 --> 00:46:15,698
Happy now?

730
00:47:08,818 --> 00:47:09,918
Do you have any idea...

731
00:47:11,928 --> 00:47:14,798
what you're doing to me and Seo Hyun?

732
00:47:16,998 --> 00:47:19,828
I know this isn't the best solution, all right?

733
00:47:20,398 --> 00:47:23,098
If it's not the best solution, then think of something else.

734
00:47:23,498 --> 00:47:25,638
This is the worst possible one.

735
00:47:25,768 --> 00:47:28,108
So, for now, let's get Seo Hyun to come back home,

736
00:47:28,178 --> 00:47:31,108
and then I'll figure something else out.

737
00:47:31,378 --> 00:47:32,978
So I'm supposed to just keep being a coward?

738
00:47:34,618 --> 00:47:36,578
Keep hiding behind you, being pathetic,

739
00:47:37,348 --> 00:47:40,688
acting loathsome and shameless?

740
00:47:40,758 --> 00:47:43,828
That's not what I'm saying, okay?

741
00:47:45,358 --> 00:47:47,328
All right. I'm sorry.

742
00:47:47,828 --> 00:47:50,928
I'm so sorry for making this decision all on my own.

743
00:47:52,368 --> 00:47:54,438
What do you have to be sorry for?

744
00:47:55,198 --> 00:47:56,698
I'm the one who should be sorry.

745
00:47:59,808 --> 00:48:01,708
To you and to Seo Hyun.

746
00:48:03,008 --> 00:48:05,948
I'm so ashamed I can't even look you in the eye.

747
00:48:06,478 --> 00:48:07,478
Honey.

748
00:48:08,378 --> 00:48:11,918
How many times do I have to tell you it's not your fault?

749
00:48:13,018 --> 00:48:14,888
If I tell her that Gyu Rim is my daughter,

750
00:48:16,318 --> 00:48:18,458
will Seo Hyun really refuse to ever see me again?

751
00:48:20,128 --> 00:48:22,398
Will she never forgive me?

752
00:48:22,998 --> 00:48:26,928
She'll say it's because I'm not her real mother, right?

753
00:48:26,998 --> 00:48:27,998
Honey.

754
00:48:30,298 --> 00:48:32,938
Let's just wait 1 year. Just 1 year, okay?

755
00:48:33,468 --> 00:48:36,878
In that time, Seo Hyun can forget all about Mu Jin,

756
00:48:36,938 --> 00:48:38,448
and maybe she'll meet someone else and fall in love.

757
00:48:38,508 --> 00:48:41,578
If that happens, we can tell her the whole truth then.

758
00:48:41,648 --> 00:48:43,548
So please, just for one year.

759
00:48:43,748 --> 00:48:46,518
What if her feelings haven't changed after one year?

760
00:48:47,358 --> 00:48:49,988
Are you going to keep living away from home?

761
00:48:53,158 --> 00:48:56,058
How can you suggest something so ridiculous?

762
00:48:58,928 --> 00:48:59,968
Honey.

763
00:49:07,908 --> 00:49:09,538
I thought you'd already left.

764
00:49:17,118 --> 00:49:18,118
Seo Hyun.

765
00:49:21,088 --> 00:49:22,888
Your mother hasn't eaten anything today.

766
00:49:24,028 --> 00:49:25,028
Just letting you know.

767
00:49:59,088 --> 00:50:00,088
Mom.

768
00:50:09,698 --> 00:50:10,738
Are you mad at me?

769
00:50:20,108 --> 00:50:22,678
Are you mad that I kicked Dad out?

770
00:50:34,428 --> 00:50:35,898
You can't forgive him.

771
00:50:38,528 --> 00:50:40,168
You can't forgive Dad.

772
00:50:40,368 --> 00:50:41,368
Seo Hyun.

773
00:50:41,598 --> 00:50:42,838
If you forgive Dad easily...

774
00:50:42,898 --> 00:50:44,708
and just let this go like it's nothing,

775
00:50:45,108 --> 00:50:46,168
I won't see you either, Mom.

776
00:50:57,818 --> 00:51:01,388
I know Go Yoon Hee is softhearted and a total pushover.

777
00:51:04,158 --> 00:51:05,628
But not this time.

778
00:51:06,588 --> 00:51:07,628
Not this time.

779
00:51:08,858 --> 00:51:10,298
You know what I mean, right?

780
00:51:30,378 --> 00:51:31,688
My, my.

781
00:51:31,748 --> 00:51:36,258
Look at you, having the romance of the century.

782
00:51:38,888 --> 00:51:41,558
Gosh, I really need to find a new regular bar.

783
00:51:41,628 --> 00:51:42,998
I told you not to come, so why are you here?

784
00:51:43,558 --> 00:51:46,298
How could I miss a show this fun over the phone?

785
00:51:47,468 --> 00:51:49,198
- On the rocks. - Yes.

786
00:51:49,198 --> 00:51:50,268
One more.

787
00:51:51,008 --> 00:51:53,768
What kind of a comedy is this?

788
00:51:54,378 --> 00:51:57,008
I'm so tired from laughing that I'm about to throw up.

789
00:51:57,408 --> 00:51:58,408
Gosh.

790
00:52:00,878 --> 00:52:01,878
Hey.

791
00:52:01,948 --> 00:52:04,388
You're getting what you deserve, you punk.

792
00:52:05,688 --> 00:52:09,158
This is your punishment for rejecting me 40 years ago.

793
00:52:12,958 --> 00:52:13,958
What?

794
00:52:14,028 --> 00:52:15,098
I guess you don't remember.

795
00:52:15,828 --> 00:52:16,828
Hey.

796
00:52:16,998 --> 00:52:19,128
If you had accepted my proposal back then,

797
00:52:19,198 --> 00:52:22,198
Mu Jin could have actually been your son.

798
00:52:25,708 --> 00:52:27,878
It wasn't 40 years ago. It was 36 years ago.

799
00:52:28,108 --> 00:52:29,338
So you do remember.

800
00:52:32,778 --> 00:52:34,118
After you rejected me,

801
00:52:34,948 --> 00:52:36,148
in a fit of rage,

802
00:52:36,978 --> 00:52:39,548
I married the man my parents chose for me.

803
00:52:40,148 --> 00:52:41,218
Without any love.

804
00:52:43,958 --> 00:52:45,428
Hey, let's get the story straight.

805
00:52:46,058 --> 00:52:47,188
How was that a proposal?

806
00:52:47,428 --> 00:52:49,628
You were drunk and harassed me all night.

807
00:52:49,798 --> 00:52:50,798
Remember now?

808
00:52:51,228 --> 00:52:53,728
Hey, go home. Go on, get cleaned up and go to sleep.

809
00:52:54,098 --> 00:52:55,168
Hey.

810
00:52:56,038 --> 00:52:58,708
Since things have come to this, how about we get married?

811
00:52:59,208 --> 00:53:00,338
It would be your third time, you know.

812
00:53:00,568 --> 00:53:01,878
So I'd be the one losing out.

813
00:53:02,608 --> 00:53:03,608
What do you say?

814
00:53:05,948 --> 00:53:06,948
You're not laughing.

815
00:53:07,578 --> 00:53:09,018
I came here to make you laugh.

816
00:53:15,288 --> 00:53:16,288
Well,

817
00:53:17,158 --> 00:53:18,228
forget it.

818
00:53:18,758 --> 00:53:21,158
It's not like you're in the mood to laugh anyway.

819
00:53:35,408 --> 00:53:36,408
Hey.

820
00:53:38,248 --> 00:53:39,248
Hey.

821
00:53:39,308 --> 00:53:40,978
I tell you to laugh, and you laugh that hard?

822
00:53:42,318 --> 00:53:43,778
Hey, people are staring.

823
00:53:45,318 --> 00:53:46,448
I mean, Mu Jin? My son?

824
00:53:48,558 --> 00:53:49,558
Unbelievable.

825
00:53:50,188 --> 00:53:52,028
You're saying such ridiculous things...

826
00:53:54,158 --> 00:53:55,528
Does this even make sense?

827
00:53:57,668 --> 00:53:59,568
What? Hey.

828
00:54:02,138 --> 00:54:03,168
Are you crying?

829
00:54:05,438 --> 00:54:07,778
Can you imagine how hard this is for Yoon Hee right now?

830
00:54:09,638 --> 00:54:11,178
I told her I would take care of everything...

831
00:54:11,248 --> 00:54:12,308
but this...

832
00:54:14,548 --> 00:54:17,748
Imagine how awkward and troubled Yoon Hee must feel right now.

833
00:54:20,518 --> 00:54:21,618
Oh, my gosh.

834
00:54:24,158 --> 00:54:27,598
You really are having the romance of the century.

835
00:54:27,658 --> 00:54:28,658
Jang Hoon Tae.

836
00:54:30,428 --> 00:54:31,568
Just go.

837
00:54:46,848 --> 00:54:47,848
What's this?

838
00:54:48,818 --> 00:54:49,948
Wow, you're so good at drawing.

839
00:54:50,988 --> 00:54:52,388
Our Gyeol is a regular Picasso.

840
00:55:00,688 --> 00:55:01,698
Hello?

841
00:55:06,568 --> 00:55:07,568
Oh, Gyu Min.

842
00:55:08,338 --> 00:55:09,338
Mister.

843
00:55:10,798 --> 00:55:12,568
Did you ask my sister?

844
00:55:14,508 --> 00:55:17,038
If the babies were switched at the hospital?

845
00:55:17,178 --> 00:55:18,908
I've been wondering about it too.

846
00:55:19,478 --> 00:55:21,678
No, I haven't asked.

847
00:55:23,048 --> 00:55:24,488
When are you going to ask her?

848
00:55:26,418 --> 00:55:27,418
I don't know.

849
00:55:29,188 --> 00:55:30,258
What if...

850
00:55:32,428 --> 00:55:34,228
What if Gyeol was the one who was switched?

851
00:55:36,158 --> 00:55:37,158
I don't know.

852
00:55:37,768 --> 00:55:39,268
Do they switch them back then?

853
00:55:40,568 --> 00:55:41,668
Like in the dramas?

854
00:55:42,138 --> 00:55:43,298
Do they just swap them...

855
00:55:43,368 --> 00:55:45,038
and send them back to their birth parents?

856
00:55:46,208 --> 00:55:47,608
That's getting a little ahead of yourself.

857
00:55:48,378 --> 00:55:49,838
That kind of thing doesn't really happen...

858
00:55:49,908 --> 00:55:50,908
in the real world.

859
00:55:51,008 --> 00:55:52,408
It does happen in real life.

860
00:55:53,548 --> 00:55:54,918
I saw it on the news.

861
00:55:56,148 --> 00:55:58,988
Listen, Gyu Min, I'm with Gyeol right now.

862
00:55:59,748 --> 00:56:03,288
Oh, okay. I'll let you go then.

863
00:56:03,758 --> 00:56:05,888
- Okay. - Sir.

864
00:56:06,558 --> 00:56:07,558
Yes?

865
00:56:11,568 --> 00:56:12,668
What if...

866
00:56:13,228 --> 00:56:15,098
my sister really did give birth,

867
00:56:15,698 --> 00:56:17,498
and her baby was switched with Gyeol at the hospital?

868
00:56:19,668 --> 00:56:21,308
What would you do then, sir?

869
00:56:26,008 --> 00:56:28,348
Gyeol is calling me, so I have to go.

870
00:56:28,648 --> 00:56:29,648
Let's hang up.

871
00:56:38,188 --> 00:56:40,058
Give it here, you rotten kid.

872
00:56:40,128 --> 00:56:42,998
- Hurry up and bring it here. - Then write me a contract.

873
00:56:43,428 --> 00:56:44,798
Write a contract promising you won't...

874
00:56:44,868 --> 00:56:47,198
kick Gyu Rim's family out and will let them keep living there.

875
00:56:48,038 --> 00:56:50,138
- My gosh. - You gutless fool.

876
00:56:50,568 --> 00:56:55,178
Those girls teamed up and completely ruined your life,

877
00:56:55,638 --> 00:56:57,948
and you gave them affection, love, and your heart.

878
00:56:58,078 --> 00:57:01,218
You even gave them money. They took a perfectly good man...

879
00:57:01,278 --> 00:57:03,918
and turned him into a total moron.

880
00:57:04,618 --> 00:57:07,548
How can you not feel wronged or angry?

881
00:57:07,718 --> 00:57:10,088
It doesn't bother me.

882
00:57:10,858 --> 00:57:12,928
Money comes and goes.

883
00:57:12,988 --> 00:57:14,958
And it's not like I'll die without it.

884
00:57:15,128 --> 00:57:16,358
Gyu Young didn't make her do anything.

885
00:57:16,428 --> 00:57:18,168
And especially Gyu Rim, she wasn't the one who dumped me.

886
00:57:18,228 --> 00:57:20,128
How many times do I have to tell you I'm the one who dumped her?

887
00:57:20,198 --> 00:57:22,338
My, my. We have a living saint here.

888
00:57:22,768 --> 00:57:23,798
Yes, that's right.

889
00:57:24,068 --> 00:57:27,338
I shouldn't have bothered going all the way to some remote temple.

890
00:57:27,708 --> 00:57:29,578
I should just pray to you instead.

891
00:57:30,138 --> 00:57:31,748
Oh, dear Buddha.

892
00:57:32,308 --> 00:57:36,548
My one and only son, who's worse than an enemy.

893
00:57:36,618 --> 00:57:39,648
I can't kill him, and I can't let him live.

894
00:57:39,718 --> 00:57:41,018
What should I do?

895
00:57:42,788 --> 00:57:44,758
Oh, foolish mortal.

896
00:57:45,428 --> 00:57:47,658
Your son's words are my words.

897
00:57:47,728 --> 00:57:50,458
So just write the contract like that punk says...

898
00:57:50,528 --> 00:57:53,428
and stop bothering poor Gyu Rim.

899
00:57:54,028 --> 00:57:57,298
- You infuriating punk. - Where should I put this up?

900
00:57:57,368 --> 00:57:59,508
Where can I put this so people will see it best...

901
00:57:59,568 --> 00:58:01,738
and the rumors will spread quickly?

902
00:58:02,008 --> 00:58:06,348
- Over there. Hey, Min Guk. - Where are you going with that?

903
00:58:06,448 --> 00:58:07,648
- Hey. - You brat.

904
00:58:07,708 --> 00:58:09,918
Your shop's the neighborhood hangout, right?

905
00:58:09,978 --> 00:58:11,718
I hear all the ladies hang out here.

906
00:58:11,788 --> 00:58:13,588
Yes, that's true, but...

907
00:58:13,648 --> 00:58:15,418
- What are you planning? - Hey.

908
00:58:15,488 --> 00:58:16,688
So what if it's the neighborhood hangout?

909
00:58:16,758 --> 00:58:19,588
Hey, put this up in your shop for me, okay?

910
00:58:19,658 --> 00:58:22,898
Are you trying to bury your own mother alive?

911
00:58:22,998 --> 00:58:24,058
Where are you going? Hey.

912
00:58:24,128 --> 00:58:25,298
Right there.

913
00:58:25,468 --> 00:58:29,138
- That's the most visible spot. - Hey. Son.

914
00:58:29,198 --> 00:58:31,208
- Let go. He's my son. - Hey, Min Guk.

915
00:58:41,008 --> 00:58:42,048
The truth...

916
00:58:43,648 --> 00:58:46,718
Being honest may not always be the right thing,

917
00:58:48,018 --> 00:58:51,088
and it might hurt someone or even be cruel,

918
00:58:52,958 --> 00:58:55,028
but I think it's better than lying and avoiding it.

919
00:58:55,598 --> 00:58:56,698
Don't be afraid.

920
00:59:04,938 --> 00:59:06,638
Study to improve...

921
00:59:07,508 --> 00:59:10,178
your skills. Outside the win...

922
00:59:13,078 --> 00:59:14,348
You've gotten them all right so far.

923
00:59:15,648 --> 00:59:17,318
Gyeol, you're so smart.

924
00:59:18,218 --> 00:59:20,188
I used to be really good at this stuff when I was younger.

925
00:59:25,228 --> 00:59:26,728
Just saying.

926
00:59:28,428 --> 00:59:29,498
Okay, on to the next problem.

927
00:59:31,798 --> 00:59:34,698
Do you want something to drink? I can make you some soy milk.

928
00:59:35,938 --> 00:59:36,938
No, thank you.

929
00:59:36,998 --> 00:59:38,638
I already brushed my teeth.

930
00:59:43,808 --> 00:59:46,108
What should I use for the next one?

931
00:59:46,948 --> 00:59:48,018
You got a text, Gyeol.

932
00:59:48,178 --> 00:59:49,478
My phone's in my room.

933
00:59:50,778 --> 00:59:53,988
People who are together and apart...

934
00:59:55,558 --> 00:59:56,718
(Han Gyu Rim)

935
00:59:56,788 --> 00:59:59,028
I'm outside your place, Mu Jin.

936
00:59:59,258 --> 01:00:00,588
Can we talk for a minute?

937
01:00:04,398 --> 01:00:05,998
Gyeol, I have to step out for a minute.

938
01:00:06,068 --> 01:00:07,428
You keep working on your problems.

939
01:00:08,098 --> 01:00:09,238
Jung Woo will be here soon.

940
01:00:09,998 --> 01:00:10,998
Okay.

941
01:00:11,808 --> 01:00:13,038
Don't worry about me.

942
01:00:13,708 --> 01:00:15,308
Go do what you need to do.

943
01:00:15,538 --> 01:00:18,408
Just pretend I'm not here.

944
01:00:21,008 --> 01:00:22,148
Okay.

945
01:00:26,148 --> 01:00:27,348
This is it.

946
01:00:28,018 --> 01:00:29,618
Following all of these...

947
01:00:38,298 --> 01:00:39,298
Han Gyu Rim.

948
01:00:45,638 --> 01:00:47,368
Gyeol's inside doing his workbook.

949
01:00:47,908 --> 01:00:50,308
Jung Woo will be here soon, so you don't have to worry.

950
01:00:56,048 --> 01:00:57,378
Should we go to a coffee shop?

951
01:00:58,148 --> 01:00:59,148
No,

952
01:00:59,718 --> 01:01:00,948
let's talk here.

953
01:01:38,028 --> 01:01:39,158
I can wait...

954
01:01:40,728 --> 01:01:42,898
all night,

955
01:01:44,358 --> 01:01:46,528
so take your time.

956
01:01:53,668 --> 01:01:54,878
Gyeol...

957
01:01:57,638 --> 01:02:00,608
He's not my biological son.

958
01:02:05,448 --> 01:02:07,148
He's my friend's son.

959
01:02:09,758 --> 01:02:11,828
My friend wasn't able to raise him...

960
01:02:14,328 --> 01:02:17,428
so I raised him.

961
01:02:22,638 --> 01:02:25,108
You told me to be honest and face things head-on,

962
01:02:28,008 --> 01:02:29,138
so with Gyeol,

963
01:02:30,308 --> 01:02:32,008
I'm going to tell him the truth.

964
01:02:36,378 --> 01:02:38,218
But I'm a bit scared.

965
01:02:39,788 --> 01:02:41,048
To be honest,

966
01:02:42,688 --> 01:02:43,958
not just a bit...

967
01:02:47,358 --> 01:02:48,858
I'm terrified.

968
01:03:08,918 --> 01:03:11,018
Let's go get something to drink.

969
01:03:11,918 --> 01:03:13,288
I'm suddenly really thirsty.

970
01:03:46,488 --> 01:03:47,488
You did the right thing.

971
01:03:49,418 --> 01:03:50,758
It's the right decision.

972
01:03:53,558 --> 01:03:57,028
Gyeol is smart and a very thoughtful kid.

973
01:03:58,028 --> 01:03:59,428
He'll understand.

974
01:04:07,608 --> 01:04:09,808
Even so, if Gyeol has a hard time...

975
01:04:11,178 --> 01:04:14,778
I'll be right there to do my best to help him through it.

976
01:04:19,088 --> 01:04:20,088
Thank you.

977
01:04:23,788 --> 01:04:26,028
I'm on a break from work, so I have to get back.

978
01:04:27,228 --> 01:04:28,328
I have to go.

979
01:04:32,098 --> 01:04:33,468
Where's your child?

980
01:04:45,348 --> 01:04:46,608
The one you gave birth to...

981
01:04:51,948 --> 01:04:53,448
Our child...

982
01:04:55,458 --> 01:04:56,688
Where is our child then?

983
01:05:32,488 --> 01:05:33,858
(Love on the Menu)

984
01:05:33,928 --> 01:05:35,758
Mr. Mu Jin wants to come see you.

985
01:05:35,828 --> 01:05:37,298
He's desperate to, right now.

986
01:05:37,358 --> 01:05:38,698
I miss Mom.

987
01:05:38,868 --> 01:05:41,638
I miss her, but I don't want to see her.

988
01:05:41,698 --> 01:05:44,368
Your father lied because of me.

989
01:05:44,638 --> 01:05:45,868
Eight years ago,

990
01:05:45,938 --> 01:05:48,738
- why did you run out on me? - I never ran away.

991
01:05:48,938 --> 01:05:50,108
You're the one who ran away.

992
01:05:50,108 --> 01:05:51,948
If you want to, leave. Please.

993
01:05:52,008 --> 01:05:53,408
And take all the kids with you.

994
01:05:53,678 --> 01:05:56,878
There's someone Gyu Rim shouldn't be seeing.

995
01:05:57,218 --> 01:05:58,948
Should we go somewhere no one knows us...

996
01:05:59,018 --> 01:06:00,488
and live there, the three of us?

